Turn Picasso96 (uaegfx) RTG on

PICASSO96 was commented out in retrodep/sysconfig.h, so picasso96.c and gfxboard.c each
compiled to an empty object and the core had no graphics card of any kind. Turning it on is one
line; everything else in this part of the series is what has to be true for that line to build
and work.

UAEGFX_INTERNAL stays off. It makes filesys.c serve libs:picasso96/uaegfx.card out of the
emulator, which only matters for a guest that has no Picasso96 installed at all - and such a
guest has no Picasso96 libraries either, so the card alone gets it nowhere.

The new source is retrodep/picasso_host.c: the libretro side of the Picasso96 platform layer,
installed by the @install-picasso-host phase. See patches/picasso96/picasso_host.c.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

--- a/retrodep/sysconfig.h
+++ b/retrodep/sysconfig.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 #define CPUEMU_40 /* generic 680x0 with JIT direct memory access */
 #define CPUEMU_50 /* generic 680x0 with indirect memory access */
 #define ACTION_REPLAY /* Action Replay 1/2/3 support */
-//#define PICASSO96 /* Picasso96 display card emulation */
+#define PICASSO96 /* Picasso96 display card emulation */ /* PEEKaboo: on, uaegfx RTG */
 //#define UAEGFX_INTERNAL /* built-in libs:picasso96/uaegfx.card */
 #define BSDSOCKET /* bsdsocket.library emulation */ /* PEEKaboo: on, POSIX and Winsock */
 #define CAPS /* CAPS-image support */
--- a/Makefile.common
+++ b/Makefile.common
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@
 	$(RETRODEP)/parser.c \
 	$(RETRODEP)/adm_hostio.c \
 	$(RETRODEP)/serial_host.c \
+	$(RETRODEP)/picasso_host.c \
 	$(RETRODEP)/machdep/support.c \
 	$(RETRODEP)/sounddep/sound.c \
 	$(RETRODEP)/threaddep/thread.c
